<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>scverse conference 2026 on scverse</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/</link><description>Recent content in scverse conference 2026 on scverse</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://scverse.org/conference2026/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Speakers</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/speakers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/speakers/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="keynote-speakers"&gt;Keynote speakers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are delighted to announce the following speakers for scverse conference 2026, with more to be confirmed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="speaker-grid"&gt;
 &lt;div class="speaker-card"&gt;
 &lt;img class="speaker-photo" src="https://scverse.org/img/events/conference2026/speakers/phil-ewels.webp" alt="Phil Ewels" /&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;Phil Ewels&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;p class="speaker-affiliation"&gt;Seqera&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;p class="speaker-bio"&gt;Product Manager for Open Source at Seqera, with a PhD in Molecular Biology from the University of Cambridge. He previously worked at the National Genomics Infrastructure (SciLifeLab, Stockholm) and the Babraham Institute in Cambridge. Phil co-founded the nf-core community and authored MultiQC, RustQC, and SRA-Explorer, and is a passionate advocate for user-friendly open-source software.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Schedule</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/schedule/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/schedule/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="program-at-a-glance"&gt;Program at a glance&lt;/h2&gt;
