&lt;h2 id="keynote-talks"&gt;Keynote talks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="ai-for-image-based-systems-biology-from-cryo-electron-tomography-to-virtual-spatial-transcriptomics"&gt;AI for Image-based Systems Biology: From Cryo-Electron Tomography to Virtual Spatial Transcriptomics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tingying Peng&lt;/strong&gt; · Helmholtz Munich&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Registration</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/registration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/registration/</guid><description>&lt;div class="status-banner"&gt;Registration is now open — &lt;a href="https://dtu.events/scverse2026/signup.html?step=participants"&gt;sign up here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="registration"&gt;Registration&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Registration for scverse conference 2026 is now open. &lt;a href="https://dtu.events/scverse2026/signup.html?step=participants"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Register here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Capacity is limited, so we recommend registering early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sign up for announcements via &lt;a href="https://scverse.zulipchat.com/"&gt;Zulip&lt;/a&gt; or follow us on social media for the latest updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="travel-grants"&gt;Travel grants&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to making the conference accessible to as many people as possible. As in previous years, we plan to offer &lt;strong&gt;travel grants&lt;/strong&gt; to help cover registration, accommodation, and travel.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Call for proposals</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/call-for-proposals/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/call-for-proposals/</guid><description>&lt;div class="status-banner"&gt;Abstract submission closed on &lt;strong&gt;September 7, 2026&lt;/strong&gt;. Thank you to everyone who submitted.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="share-your-work"&gt;Share your work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scverse conference program is built with the community. We welcome submissions from researchers, developers, and users across the single-cell and spatial omics ecosystem. Submission types include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="card-grid"&gt;
 &lt;div class="info-card"&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;Talks&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Present your research, tool, or method as a contributed talk. Selected abstracts are scheduled across the main program.&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="info-card"&gt;
 &lt;h3&gt;Posters&lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Share work in progress and connect with the community during dedicated poster sessions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sponsors</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/sponsors/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/sponsors/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="partner-with-scverse"&gt;Partner with scverse&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;scverse® builds the foundational, interoperable open-source tools for single-cell and spatial omics — including &lt;strong&gt;Scanpy, AnnData, squidpy, and scvi-tools&lt;/strong&gt; — used by labs worldwide and described in journals such as &lt;em&gt;Nature Biotechnology&lt;/em&gt;. scverse is a non-profit, fiscally sponsored project of &lt;a href="https://numfocus.org/project/scverse"&gt;NumFOCUS&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual scverse conference sits at the &lt;strong&gt;intersection of academia and industry&lt;/strong&gt;, bringing together developers, academic labs, and researchers at every career stage. Your sponsorship funds the community directly — travel grants, fee waivers, and free tools, not shareholders.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Venue &amp; travel</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/travel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/travel/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;scverse conference 2026 · DTU Lyngby Campus, Kongens Lyngby · 12–14 October 2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-venue"&gt;The venue&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class="venue-addr"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DTU Lyngby Campus, Building 101&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Address: Anker Engelunds Vej 1, 2800 Kgs. Lyngby, Denmark.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="travel-map"&gt;&lt;iframe title="Map of DTU Lyngby Campus" loading="lazy" src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=Anker%20Engelunds%20Vej%201,%202800%20Kongens%20Lyngby&amp;z=14&amp;output=embed"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The campus sits about 15 km north of central Copenhagen, in Kongens Lyngby. There are two sensible approaches: stay locally in Lyngby, which gives you a short walk to the venue and quiet evenings, or stay in Copenhagen and travel in each morning, which takes roughly 40 minutes. Both work well. Lyngby has very few hotels, so if you want to be within walking distance, book early.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Code of Conduct</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/code-of-conduct/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/code-of-conduct/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This code of conduct was developed for the scverse conferences. For more details, see the full &lt;a href="https://scverse.org/about/code_of_conduct"&gt;scverse Code of Conduct&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="our-pledge"&gt;Our pledge&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We as members, contributors, and leaders pledge to make participation in our community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex characteristics, gender identity and expression, level of experience, education, socio-economic status, nationality, personal appearance, race, caste, color, religion, or sexual identity and orientation.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Organizers</title><link>https://scverse.org/conference2026/organizers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://scverse.org/conference2026/organizers/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="organizing-committee"&gt;Organizing committee&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scverse conference 2026 is organized by members of the &lt;a href="https://scverse.org/people"&gt;scverse community&lt;/a&gt;, together with our local partners at DTU, Copenhagen. scverse is a community-developed, non-profit project, fiscally sponsored by &lt;a href="https://numfocus.org/project/scverse"&gt;NumFOCUS&lt;/a&gt;. The conference is run by the people who build and maintain the ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
